tuxamp (0.1.1~alpha) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New: cast / stream to smart devices on the local network. Supports
    Google Cast (Chromecast, Google and Nest speakers and speaker groups,
    Android TV / Google TV) and DLNA renderers (smart TVs, Sonos, Kodi).
    Right-click > Cast to device... or Ctrl+Shift+C.
  * Playback controls, the volume slider, EQ and balance all work while
    casting; the visualizers follow the device.
  * README: new "Casting to smart devices" section; corrected the startup
    voice line.
  * See BUGFIXES.md for the bug fixed in this release.

 -- Shawn Rapaz <shawnrapaz@gmail.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:15:36 +0900

tuxamp (0.1.0~alpha) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release of TuxAmp, a Winamp 2.x-style music player for Linux:
    main window, 10-band equalizer and playlist editor, smoothly zoomable
    together by dragging the bottom-right corner.
  * TuxDrop: a full-screen, music-reactive visualizer with 9 presets, beat
    detection and automatic preset cycling.
  * Icons: Tux the penguin holding a lightning bolt.
  * Startup voice: "TuxAmp, it really whips the penguin's ass!"
  * See BUGFIXES.md for the bugs fixed during development.

